2.1.26 Where a SAR Authority has overall coordination of a SAR operation, the SMC shall give 
particular attention to the following matters as relevant to the search:  
a) In conjunction with the meteorological office, keeping a watch on weather conditions in 
the probability area, routes used by SAR assets in transit to and from the search area and 
at aerodromes used as bases or alternate aerodromes for search aircraft;  
b) Coordination of search aircraft in the light of operational conditions by diverting or 
recalling aircraft or reassigning search areas as conditions dictate; 
c) Planning so as to minimise conflict between search aircraft in adjoining areas;




